Q33: Explain the difference between dBFS and dBm in two sentences.
---
dBFS (decibels relative to full scale) is a unit used in digital systems to measure signal power relative to the maximum possible value, where 0 dBFS represents the absolute maximum level and any value above it indicates clipping. In contrast, dBm (decibels relative to 1 milliwatt) is an absolute power unit used in analog and RF systems that measures signal strength relative to a fixed physical reference of 1 mW, independent of the system's maximum capacity.<|im_end|>
